status LED: blink (heartbeat) in Linux instead of solid on (R3).

The green LED (pio69) was solid: default-state="on" + diag led-boot/running
bindings (195). Heartbeat = alive (like r4-pro / openwrt-one / r4-lite). Keep
led-failsafe on green; led-upgrade stays on blue.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7986a-bananapi-bpi-r3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7986a-bananapi-bpi-r3.dts
@@ -23,9 +23,8 @@
 		serial0 = &uart0;
 		ethernet0 = &gmac0;
 		ethernet1 = &gmac1;
-		led-boot = &green_led;
+		/* green -> heartbeat (alive); keep failsafe; blue keeps led-upgrade */
 		led-failsafe = &green_led;
-		led-running = &green_led;
 		led-upgrade = &blue_led;
 	};
 
@@ -94,7 +93,7 @@
 			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_GREEN>;
 			function = LED_FUNCTION_POWER;
 			gpios = <&pio 69 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
-			default-state = "on";
+			linux,default-trigger = "heartbeat";
 		};
 
 		blue_led: led-1 {
